{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f1c2a90-3f4c-4f7a-9a1e-2b7d5c8e4a11",
    "name": "Mosaic - chapters 02-03",
    "description": "The development loop for Mosaic's single service, as chapter 2 of Federated GraphQL on .NET builds it.\n\nPoint the `baseUrl` environment variable at a running service (`dotnet run --project src/Mosaic.Api`, or `docker compose up`) and run the collection. Every request carries an assertion, so `newman run` is a smoke test as well as a demonstration.\n\nIntrospection only answers when the service runs in the Development environment. HotChocolate 16 disables it everywhere else by default.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Every product",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"no GraphQL errors\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"errors\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the seeded catalog holds 25 products\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.data.products).to.have.lengthOf(25);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "{\n  products {\n    id\n    sku\n    title\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The smallest useful query. If this fails, nothing else in the collection is worth reading."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "A product page",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"no GraphQL errors\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"errors\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "const product = body.data.productById;",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Catalog answered\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(product.sku).to.eql(\"MOS-FRN-0001\");",
              "    pm.expect(product.title).to.be.a(\"string\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Pricing answered\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(product.price.amount).to.be.a(\"number\");",
              "    pm.expect(product.price.currency).to.eql(\"EUR\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Inventory answered\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(product.availableQuantity).to.be.a(\"number\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Reviews answered, and reached into Accounts for each author\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(product.reviews).to.be.an(\"array\").that.is.not.empty;",
              "    pm.expect(product.reviews[0].author.displayName).to.be.a(\"string\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "query ProductPage($id: ID!) {\n  productById(id: $id) {\n    id\n    sku\n    title\n    description\n    category\n    price {\n      amount\n      currency\n    }\n    availableQuantity\n    averageRating\n    reviews {\n      rating\n      body\n      createdAt\n      author {\n        displayName\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{\n  \"id\": \"a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\"\n}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "One request assembled from four domains: Catalog owns the identity, Pricing the price, Inventory the stock, Reviews the opinions, and Reviews in turn asks Accounts who wrote each one. This is the query chapter 1 promised and the one the whole book pulls apart.\n\nWatch the service log while this runs. The lookup count it prints is the honest cost of doing it this way."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "One product, by variable",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"no GraphQL errors\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"errors\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the variable selected the product we asked for\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.data.productBySku.sku).to.eql(\"MOS-KIT-0001\");",
              "    pm.expect(body.data.productBySku.title).to.eql(\"Ridge Chef's Knife\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "query BySku($sku: String!) {\n  productBySku(sku: $sku) {\n    id\n    sku\n    title\n    price {\n      amount\n      currency\n    }\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{\n  \"sku\": \"MOS-KIT-0001\"\n}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The same document, reused with a different variable. Editing the Variables pane rather than the query is the habit worth forming: the document stays constant, which is what makes persisted operations possible later."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "A field that does not exist",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"rejected before execution with 400\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the error names the field and the type\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an(\"array\").that.is.not.empty;",
              "    pm.expect(body.errors[0].message).to.include(\"nope\");",
              "    pm.expect(body.errors[0].extensions.type).to.eql(\"Product\");",
              "    pm.expect(body.errors[0].extensions.field).to.eql(\"nope\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"nothing was resolved\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"data\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "{\n  products {\n    nope\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "A deliberate mistake, kept in the collection because the failure is worth seeing. Validation runs against the schema before a single resolver is called, so no data comes back at all, and the error points at the GraphQL specification rather than carrying a HotChocolate error code."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Introspection",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"introspection is answering\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.data.__schema.queryType.name).to.eql(\"Query\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the schema carries the types chapter 2 built\", function () {",
              "    const names = body.data.__schema.types.map(function (t) { return t.name; });",
              "    [\"Product\", \"Money\", \"Review\", \"Customer\", \"Order\", \"OrderLine\"].forEach(function (n) {",
              "        pm.expect(names).to.include(n);",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "{\n  __schema {\n    queryType {\n      name\n    }\n    types {\n      name\n    }\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The query Postman itself runs when it fetches a schema, written out by hand so you can see what the tooling is doing.\n\nThis is also the request that fails first when the service is not running in Development: HotChocolate 16 disables introspection outside it by default, and the answer becomes an HC0046 error rather than a schema."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Cost analysis, without executing",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "// GraphQL-Cost: validate stops the request at the cost analyzer, which is",
              "// the seventh middleware in the pipeline. Nothing after it runs.",
              "pm.test(\"no data came back, because nothing was executed\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"data\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the cost analyzer reported its numbers\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.extensions.operationCost.fieldCost).to.eql(30);",
              "    pm.expect(body.extensions.operationCost.typeCost).to.eql(4);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "GraphQL-Cost",
            "value": "validate"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "{\n  products {\n    title\n    reviews {\n      rating\n      author {\n        displayName\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
            "variables": "{}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The catalog-with-reviews query, sent with the GraphQL-Cost: validate header. The request is parsed, validated and costed, then stops: there is no data key at all. Three async resolver fields at the default weight of 10 make a field cost of 30. Chapter 3 uses this to show that a request can leave the pipeline from the middle of it."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "A document that does not parse",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"responds 400\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"the error is a syntax error\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.errors[0].extensions.code).to.eql(\"HC0011\");",
              "});",
              "",
              "// Compare with \"A field that does not exist\", which carries no code but",
              "// does carry specifiedBy. Two rejections, two different shapes, and they",
              "// come from two different layers of the server.",
              "pm.test(\"there is no data key\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"data\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "graphql",
          "graphql": {
            "query": "{\n  products {\n    title\n",
            "variables": "{}"
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/graphql",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "graphql"
          ]
        },
        "description": "An unclosed brace. This never reaches the execution pipeline: the ASP.NET Core transport parses the document before the pipeline runs, so the request is rejected there and no diagnostic listener ever sees it. Chapter 3 measures that."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5100",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ]
}
